<title>BELGIUM: ENGRAIS ROSIER 1996 PROFIT RISES 7 PCT.</title>
<headline>ENGRAIS ROSIER 1996 PROFIT RISES 7 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to December 31,</p>
<p>1996 (in millions of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net per share (francs)	 447  vs   419</p>
<p>    Net dividend (francs)	  165  vs   150</p>
<p>    Group net profit		 114  vs   107</p>
<p>    Pre-tax current net profit   190  vs   176</p>
<p>    Cons turnover/sales	  2,462  vs 2,380</p>
<p>    Cash flow			  156  vs   151</p>
<p>NOTE - Engrais-Rosier is a Belgian chemical fertilizer maker</p>
<p>which also has interests in grain collection and storage.</p>
<p>In a statement, the company said deliveries so far this year</p>
<p>were in line with 1996 levels. Prospects for the second half of</p>
<p>the year were unclear because of uncertainties surrounding</p>
<p>European Union agricultural policy for the 1997/1998 planting</p>
<p>year. &quot;The consequences on consumption of fertilizers are</p>
<p>difficult to predict today,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>Globally, use of fertilizers should remain firm due to</p>
<p>growing demand, it said.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax</p>
<p>+32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
